.TH "PB-PREVIEW-STATUS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview-status - Show temporary preview status


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview status <preview> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show temporary preview status

.PP
Show the selected preview's current publication and connector state. A URL existing in the account is distinct from a ready, reachable origin.

.PP
A preview exposes a local target through a temporary Paperboat URL or private/team access policy. Inspect its status before sharing the URL, and stop or delete it when no longer needed. Browser HTTP terminates TLS at the edge.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the canonical preview resource as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-preview(1)\fP
